virglrenderer: Venus render passes, framebuffers and begins stay inside the pass

What: a render pass's attachment references (color, input, resolve,
depth/stencil, depth/stencil resolve, fragment shading rate, preserve) name
its attachments or UNUSED; colors per subpass within maxColorAttachments; the
bind point is graphics; attachment sample counts are ones the device has;
dependencies name its subpasses; VkRenderPassMultiviewCreateInfo has a mask per
subpass (or none) and an offset per dependency (or none); input attachment
aspects name a subpass and one of its inputs; resolve modes are known. vkr
keeps each pass's attachment count, the clear values a begin must give (up to
the last attachment whose load op clears, or whose stencil load op clears on
a depth/stencil format: Vulkan ignores a color attachment's) and a table of
its subpasses (colors, view mask). A framebuffer has the pass's
attachment count (imageless: its image info count), no NULL view, a size
within the device's limits. A begin names a framebuffer of the pass's
attachments, enough clear values, imageless views, sample locations for its
attachments and subpasses. Dynamic rendering: colors within the limit, layers
within maxFramebufferLayers, a resolve view where an attachment with a view
sets a resolve mode (Vulkan asks for none without a view). A
secondary inherits a subpass the pass has. Multiview: KosmicKrisp's
maxMultiviewViewCount is told to the guest as the largest Metal vertex
amplification count the GPU supports (read once from Metal), and view masks
past it are refused where they arrive (render pass multiview info, subpass
descriptions 2, rendering info, inheritance, pipeline rendering info in the
pipeline-limits patch); correlation masks are not (no rule bounds them by
the view count, and the drivers only copy them). A refusal ends the app's
context.
Why: Mesa's vk_render_pass (KosmicKrisp, NDEBUG) indexes attachments by every
reference and the framebuffer's views by the pass's count, reads a clear value
per CLEAR attachment and a sample location per named attachment; KosmicKrisp
writes colors into arrays of 8 at begin (9 overflowed its stack: SIGABRT
__stack_chk_fail) and renders N views with a vertex amplification count of N:
Metal ends the process on 9 to 32 views on Apple7 (M1 Max) although the guest
was told 32 (legal apps).
Upstream: the multiview count is a KosmicKrisp bug (draft); the rest OmacVM
policy (spec VUIDs), draft only.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the r- cases: the multiview cases
expect refusal past the count vkr reports for the device and work up to it).

